 "title": "How fast does your money double? The Rule of 72 #shorts",
 "description": "Divide 72 by your yearly return and you get roughly how many years your money takes to double. At 4% that's 18 years, at 7% about 10, at 10% about 7.2. The exact answers (17.7, 10.2 and 7.3 years) are very close.\n\nAssumptions: returns compounded once a year; $1,000 example left untouched for 30 years. Rates are examples only: real returns vary and are not guaranteed. Not financial advice.\n\n#ruleof72 #compoundinterest #personalfinance #investing #moneytips",
